WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.419 --> 00:00:08.920
What it do soldier boy?

00:00:08.920 --> 00:00:11.600
This week
we goin to WAR with All Quiet on the Western

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:14.910
Front by Erich Maria Remarque.

00:00:14.910 --> 00:00:21.650
During WWI, Paul Baumer and his boys catch
an earful from their

00:00:21.650 --> 00:00:26.410
teacher, who tell ‘em they gotta fly they
German colors, pack a gat, and run up on dat

00:00:26.410 --> 00:00:27.660
French army.

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:31.000
After livin by the trigger in the trenches,
Paul and his boy Muller

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:34.190
hit up their homie Kemmerich, whose leg ALL
jacked up.

00:00:34.190 --> 00:00:39.079
When Kemerich up and dies, Muller scores his
fresh kicks since K-diddy ain’t gonna be

00:00:39.079 --> 00:00:40.600
needing em no mo.

00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:45.249
Back at the front, Paul and his g-
man Kat rough through all sorts of ridonkulous

00:00:45.249 --> 00:00:50.570
sh**; fools even get bombed in a graveyard
where all dat blaze slangs up the dead bodies.

00:00:50.570 --> 00:00:51.570
Ugh.. (shiver)

00:00:51.570 --> 00:00:56.219
When Paul gets leave to go back to
his trap, he realize that the war dun changed

00:00:56.219 --> 00:00:59.539
him so much that he can’t kick it in his
hood like he used to.

00:00:59.539 --> 00:01:03.109
He drops in to pay respects to his his mama
who tusslin with cancer.

00:01:03.109 --> 00:01:07.729
A little later he goes to chop game with some
Russian prisoners who he realize are just

00:01:07.729 --> 00:01:08.920
you erryday hoods.

00:01:08.920 --> 00:01:12.210
Why’s he gotta fight ‘em when he ain’t
got no real beef with ‘em?

00:01:12.210 --> 00:01:15.180
Back in the sh**, Paul gets run in
to a crater.

00:01:15.180 --> 00:01:19.360
When a Frenchy hops in with him, Paul whips
out his shank and ENDS that fool.

00:01:19.360 --> 00:01:24.259
But Paul gettin all torn up bout his deed,
cuz he went and ganked some fool he ain’t

00:01:24.259 --> 00:01:25.259
even hate!

00:01:25.259 --> 00:01:26.259
Ain’t that some bullsh**?

00:01:26.259 --> 00:01:30.280
He fesses up to Kat and his boys
but they just like “chill baby.

00:01:30.280 --> 00:01:32.020
brotha gotta do what he gotta do.”

00:01:32.020 --> 00:01:36.890
As the war goes on, Paul sees all his bruthas
drop one by one.

00:01:36.890 --> 00:01:40.859
When the Germans start backin down and
the end of the war nears, Paul don’t give

00:01:40.859 --> 00:01:43.579
a fu** cuz he all alone in the world.

00:01:43.579 --> 00:01:45.039
Then one day- POP!

00:01:45.039 --> 00:01:46.039
POP!

00:01:46.039 --> 00:01:47.770
Paul gets pumped full of lead.

00:01:47.770 --> 00:01:50.640
But it ain’t
no thang: Paul’s finally got a little peace

00:01:50.640 --> 00:01:52.840
and nobody else seems to give a damn.

00:01:52.840 --> 00:01:57.340
The report of the day simply reads: S’all
quiet on the western front.”

00:01:57.340 --> 00:02:03.979
Crews from all over da hood say this book
be da most throwed-up

00:02:03.979 --> 00:02:06.149
piece of anti-war talk out there.

00:02:06.149 --> 00:02:16.840
But for a book with so much street
cred, dem ivory tower hoods don’t give 

00:02:16.840 --> 00:02:19.440
it much respect.

00:02:19.440 --> 00:02:25.890
Then again, as some gangstas say-
all good art is born of suffering.

00:02:25.890 --> 00:02:29.760
Matter of fact, dealin with dat
post-war funk is the whole reason he wrote

00:02:29.760 --> 00:02:30.890
da book:

00:02:30.890 --> 00:02:44.000
The war don’t just ghost bruthas,
it haunts em too.

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:47.840
Just like Paul and his posse, Remarque’s
whole generation itchin to find meaning in

00:02:47.840 --> 00:02:52.489
the world, but just can’t get on that level
after beastin through the twisted-ass realities

00:02:52.489 --> 00:02:53.489
of the war.

00:02:53.489 --> 00:02:56.940
Not only are these soldier boys
alienated from anything they found meaningful

00:02:56.940 --> 00:03:02.030
before sh** went cray, but also from: who
they are, who they’ll become, and the whole

00:03:02.030 --> 00:03:03.879
world around them.

00:03:03.879 --> 00:03:21.970
With the world gone to complete
sh**, you only got time to worry bout the

00:03:21.970 --> 00:03:23.220
realest of the reals.

00:03:23.220 --> 00:03:27.470
And sometimes there ain’t nothin realer
than the bare necessities- like K- Diddy’s

00:03:27.470 --> 00:03:28.470
boots.

00:03:28.470 --> 00:03:32.280
When K-Baby buys the farm, his boy
Muller gets hooked up with a sweet pair of

00:03:32.280 --> 00:03:33.280
J’s.

00:03:33.280 --> 00:03:35.659
Then after Muller gets capped, Paul starts
rockin’ em.

00:03:35.659 --> 00:03:40.060
And it ain’t long before Paul follows the
rest of em to hang with Tupac and Biggie.

00:03:40.060 --> 00:03:44.829
Not only are them boots symbolizing the raw
realities of war, but sportin em pretty much

00:03:44.829 --> 00:03:46.750
marks yo ass for death.

00:03:46.750 --> 00:03:51.469
Paul lays down the cold truth when
he say that life is just: dystentery, shells,

00:03:51.469 --> 00:03:55.360
tanks, gas, common graves, and death.

00:03:55.360 --> 00:04:10.549
But as dark as sh** be, Paul know that he
still got one thing keepin him goin:

00:04:10.549 --> 00:04:11.549
So come on, comerade.

00:04:11.549 --> 00:04:15.540
Rep that
esprit de corps and cop some Thug Notes swag.

00:04:15.540 --> 00:04:21.570
Stay smart and hit me up next week.

00:04:21.570 --> 00:04:23.750
Peace!

